{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888590,"nonce":"yVSzfAd2hmRlodIErw0Jsx6ocE0=","title":"No user can be granted anything, so \"only an approver on this ToolServer may approve a Remedy\" has no meaning","message":"**What is wrong.** ADR 0054 §4 requires one grant — approve Remedies on a given ToolServer — as the first piece of the deferred `authz` module (SPEC §I.1, `authz` DEFERRED-POST-V1). `internal/identity/domain` has users, sessions, tokens and Slack identities and no permission model.\n\n**Why it matters.** Every 0054 slice is blocked on it.\n\n**Where.** Identity module; design review needed on how a grant is administered before any admin role exists (who grants the first grant?).\n\n**Scope.** medium.\n\n**Done when.** The owner has ruled on bootstrap (who may grant); a user can hold the grant per ToolServer; the grant is a permission only — it routes nothing and creates no queue.\n\n**Blocked by.** `2e9a086`\n\n**Mode.** HITL — needs a human decision or review before it can be implemented. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}